WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.230
“There is no elevator to success, you&nbsp;
gotta take the stairs - Zig Ziglar”.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.740
If you find meaning in quotes like this,

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.650
put them right up where you&nbsp;
will see them every day.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:13.590
Here are another 13 tips to get started.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:17.040
Ask Why!

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.380
If we don't know why we are doing it,

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.760
then we don't see a point.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.740
Whether we want to make a career,

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:26.040
change the world, or prove some idiots wrong,

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.770
these are all great reasons to get going.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.740
Simon Sinek, spoke of the Golden Circle.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:35.280
First ask WHY?, then HOW? and WHAT?.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.710
If you don't have a purpose right now,

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.500
pick up a skill that helps you once you do.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.940
Like reading fast, learning how&nbsp;
to learn or public speaking.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:48.090
Know about The Dunning Kruger Effect.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:52.350
The theory describes that&nbsp;
many of us are too confident

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:53.340
when we learn something new.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.530
Once we actually start learning,

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:59.010
we realize how difficult it&nbsp;
is and how incompetent we are.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:02.820
As a result, our motivation&nbsp;
drops and many of us quit.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:05.730
The trick to success is to keep going anyways.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:08.160
Once we master an area,

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.480
our confidence returns.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:13.710
Look For Feedback!

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:17.400
Marathon runners know that encouraging spectators

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.740
can make a massive difference on the last meters.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:23.790
Feedback is a strong force&nbsp;
so deliberately seek it.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:25.830
One way, just ask for advice.

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:29.610
Most people love giving it,&nbsp;
it makes them feel smart.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:32.310
Entrepreneurs who look for investors say

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:34.470
“Ask for money, you'll get advice."

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:36.960
"Ask for advice, you'll get money.”

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:40.410
Articulate Your Values!

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:43.920
In one experiment, at the&nbsp;
beginning of the new school year,

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.860
7th graders had to pick a personal value,

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.420
such as being good at school,

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.490
making friends or music.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:54.510
Then they spent 15 minutes writing&nbsp;
down why this mattered to them.

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:58.830
To remind them, the process&nbsp;
was repeated every 2-4 month.

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.270
Within two years,

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:04.050
most weak students saw a&nbsp;
10% increase in all grades.

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:06.870
A year later, the experiment was repeated.

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:11.100
This time, the value “being good&nbsp;
at school” was not even available.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:15.040
The surprising truth. Again,&nbsp;
all grades got better.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:18.280
Remind yourself what you really care about.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.160
Get A Mentor!

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.040
Look for charismatic people you can look up to.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:27.070
By following a mentor, we can find inspiration,

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:30.370
get new ideas, maybe even find purpose.

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:33.340
You might be able to find them around the block.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:36.520
For a list of our favorite&nbsp;
mentors, check our website,

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:38.080
or the descriptions below.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:42.430
Don’t make excuses!

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:46.960
To see if you do, Bernard Roth&nbsp;
from the Stanford's d-school

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:51.490
teaches to reframe problems by asking&nbsp;
yourself this particular question:

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:55.240
“What would it do for me if I&nbsp;
had already solved the problem?"

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:57.760
For example, if you think you're fat,

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.150
then ask yourself “What would it&nbsp;
do for me if I would lose weight?”

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:04.990
If the answer is that you would&nbsp;
ask that cute girl out on a date,

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:08.170
then forget about losing weight&nbsp;
and ask her out on a date!

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:12.610
Prime Yourself!

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:14.860
Canadian researchers observed

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:18.580
that salesmen in call centers&nbsp;
can be 50% more successful

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:21.040
when they see pictures that represent success

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:22.150
while making their calls.

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:24.580
The effect is called priming.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:27.250
Most of us become smarter in a library,

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:29.260
because we tend to be more thoughtful.

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:32.200
And many feel more successful when we dress well,

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:35.530
stand up straight with our arms&nbsp;
out and our heads held high.

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:38.500
Make Bets.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.440
Make your life a game and take bets.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.990
Groups of pretty people do that

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.790
all over the world to lose weight.

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:48.880
The one who can’t lose 2 kilos in 6 weeks

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:50.530
has to buy cupcakes for everyone.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:53.080
But it also works for reading books

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.990
or challenging yourself to&nbsp;
asking a girl out for dinner.

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:59.230
Track Your Record!

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:01.810
Records show us where we were coming from.

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:03.430
They indicate progress.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:07.480
Good music teachers record&nbsp;
the student's first lesson.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.960
One year later they show their&nbsp;
students what they recorded.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:13.720
Most are amazed how much they progressed.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.730
As Nelson Mandela said

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:18.880
“it always seems impossible until it’s done”.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.360
Start Small!

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:25.300
When we put effort into something and we succeed,

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.420
we are motivated to continue.

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:29.910
It's a self-reinforcing circle.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:32.310
If we aim too high right at the beginning,

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:34.350
it’s likely that we will fail.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:36.090
This can lead to frustration

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:38.970
and we might stop before we even get started.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:40.800
Want to learn how to sing?

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.230
Start with 5 minutes every morning.

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:46.590
Surround Yourself with Positive People!

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:50.250
Author Jim Rohn wrote that we are the average of

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:52.530
the five people we spend the most time with.

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:56.010
To get motivated spend time with positive people

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:57.000
that have a growth mindset.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:01.110
Negative people often have a&nbsp;
problem for every solution.

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:04.740
Get Context!

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:06.810
If you need to study math,

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:09.150
but your passion is sports and cooking,

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:11.490
analyze your favorite football player.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:14.400
Find out how many kilometer he runs

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.620
and how many goals he scores on average.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:19.890
Then calculate calories and make a healthy meal

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:23.100
that would give him enough energy&nbsp;
to score 2 goals in one game.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:26.340
Help Others!

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:29.640
If they succeed, you get positive energy back.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:33.240
One trick to motivate others is to use purpose.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:35.430
Explain why things matter.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.220
Paint a picture of their possible future.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:40.320
Then engage them to take responsibility.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:45.150
Last, give them the right tools&nbsp;
and feedback, to help them succeed.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:48.630
Leadership coach Steve Radcliffe calls it

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:50.610
“future, engage, deliver”.

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:54.270
Establish Discipline.

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:56.820
As motivation can come and go,

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:59.700
discipline will stay and watch you like a hawk.

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:04.110
One way to get disciplined is to&nbsp;
set a fixed time to do something

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:06.900
and then make sure you&nbsp;
always do it no matter what.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:08.340
For example:

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:12.000
Work out every morning for 20&nbsp;
minutes right before breakfast.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:15.930
Over time it will become a habit&nbsp;
and you don't even need motivation.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:21.750
If you have to do something&nbsp;
important or make a big decision,

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:24.300
switch off YouTube right now and do it.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:27.510
As internet activist Aaron Swartz asked:

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:31.320
"What is the most important thing&nbsp;
you could be working on right now?

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:34.380
And if you aren’t working&nbsp;
on that, why aren’t you?"

